# Gate A whitelist — agent-construction sites that do not reach the shared
# middleware base.
#
# EMPTY, and it should stay that way.
#
# History: 1 -> 0. `agents/factory.py` was the only entry. It was not routed
# through the shared base; it was DELETED (FR-003), because its
# middleware-takeover contract was incompatible with Article II by design —
# you cannot guarantee both "the caller controls the whole middleware list" and
# "no path bypasses policy".
#
# Gate A's rule therefore stays at its stronger form: EVERY create_agent site,
# not merely every publicly reachable one. A weaker rule would have let the
# module survive by being made private, and would not catch a new INTERNAL
# bypass added later.
#
# Every entry needs a reason. An entry deferring to future work must name the
# task that closes it, and the gate FAILS once that task lands.
